  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">An adaptation of J.R.R. Tolkien's poem Errantry weaves through Pfeiffer's illustrations.  Errantry was written in 1933 and published in his The adventures of Tom Bombadil, in 1962.  The illustrations are inspired by Kaiser Maximilian's Triumpfzug.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The scroll includes a timeline of war and conflict in the twentieth century.  At the foot of the scroll is the name of the conflict, its dates, and how many people were killed or injured.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"The scroll is housed in an actual 105mm Howitzer Artillery Brass Casing ... different types of shell casings are used for each copy of the edition"--Label inside wooden box that holds the scroll in its shell casing.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
